WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410
Petrol is a runny liquid.

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.450
Candle wax is a solid you
can hold in your hand.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.750
Yet both are mostly alkanes:
molecules of carbon and hydrogen,

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.550
joined only by single bonds.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.830
So if they belong to the same family,

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.350
why is one a runny liquid
and the other a solid?

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.630
In this mission, you'll meet the
homologous series of organic chemistry,

8
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.790
and the general formula
that fits every member.

9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.770
You'll find out what changes,
and what stays the same,

10
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.810
from one member of a series to the next.

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.990
Your mission: explain why petrol is
a liquid but candle wax is a solid.
